;; Stores whatever it is handed, so a transaction can be made to produce an account state
;; of a chosen size. The account-state ceiling is checked in the action phase, after the
;; compute phase has already set the new data, so reaching it needs a real transaction
;; rather than a helper that asks the limit what it thinks.
() recv_internal(int balance, int value, cell full_message, slice body) impure {
  set_data(body~load_ref());
}
